(633232, 63865, 12569, '<td valign="top">I would like to thank you all for placing your comments, all of them were interesting and encouraging to keep on taking photographs! Afterwards I also thought that the picture would have been more exciting if I wouldn''t be visible in the girl''s eye.<br/> <br/>Frank Herbergs</td>', 'I would like to thank you all for placing your comments, all of them were interesting and encouraging to keep on taking photographs! Afterwards I also thought that the picture would have been more exciting if I wouldn''t be visible in the girl''s eye. Frank Herbergs', '2004-03-23 09:55:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(633290, 63796, 9689, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju með fjórða sætið, það hlaut að vera að þetta væri íslensk stelpa ;)</td>', 'Til hamingju með fjórða sætið, það hlaut að vera að þetta væri íslensk stelpa ;)', '2004-03-23 10:46:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(633408, 63943, 16499, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club.<br/> <br/>For the challenge the composition is kinda doubtful. I''d love to see the edge of the paper. Textures and colors are xcellent, lighting is OK. I guess the low final score is due to the high competition in this challenge ;-)</td>', 'From Critique Club. For the challenge the composition is kinda doubtful. I''d love to see the edge of the paper. Textures and colors are xcellent, lighting is OK. I guess the low final score is due to the high competition in this challenge ;-)', '2004-03-23 12:07:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(633418, 63334, 16499, '<td valign="top">From critique club.<br/> <br/>This shot is exhibiting superb technique and knowledge of composition. The title is intriguing and fits the challenge. The only thing that leaves me uncomfortable is colors. The flower does not look "yummy" - the green cast spoils it and for the eye of a bee... The bees have a completely different than human colorspace in their vision ;-) they see green as us - grey.</td>', 'From critique club. This shot is exhibiting superb technique and knowledge of composition. The title is intriguing and fits the challenge. The only thing that leaves me uncomfortable is colors. The flower does not look "yummy" - the green cast spoils it and for the eye of a bee... The bees have a completely different than human colorspace in their vision ;-) they see green as us - grey.', '2004-03-23 12:16:08.000000', NULL, 0),
